<!--
    The launcher icon's foreground: one gill cluster, and it has no face.

    Three frond-pink dots around one paler body-pink circle
    (docs/ux/visual-identity.md §7.1), transcribed from the Gawi Redesign
    canvas on its own 108-grid with the board's 1.35 about the centre baked
    into the coordinates. VectorDrawable has no circle element, so each is
    two arcs.

    **No corrective scale, and that is the point.** A launcher shows only the
    central 72 of the 108 canvas and guarantees only the 66dp circle inside it
    — radius 33 about the centre. The right-hand dot sits at x 67 rather than
    70 so the cluster reaches 31.1 of those 33, which is why nothing has to be
    shrunk to fit. The 1.9 that leaves is also why a stalk back to a body was
    drawn and refused: a stem either runs off the frame or costs a third of
    the mark.

    Colours are the character's own (docs/ux/momo.md §2, MomoPalette), not
    theme roles — Momo is the same in both themes, the way a plush toy is. The
    ground is not: it is the light scheme's onPrimaryContainer, because a pale
    cluster on a pale ground has no contrast once the face is gone
    (gawiLauncherBackground, and §7.1 for the measurement).

    Held loosely: the mark derives from the character, so a change of Momo's
    style redraws it rather than reopening it.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
  <path
      android:fillColor="#FFF2A0B8"
      android:pathData="M27,64.8 a13.5,13.5 0 1,1 27,0 a13.5,13.5 0 1,1 -27,0 Z M37.125,43.2 a16.875,16.875 0 1,1 33.75,0 a16.875,16.875 0 1,1 -33.75,0 Z M58.05,55.35 a13.5,13.5 0 1,1 27,0 a13.5,13.5 0 1,1 -27,0 Z" />
  <path
      android:fillColor="#FFF7C3D1"
      android:pathData="M47.925,62.1 a10.125,10.125 0 1,1 20.25,0 a10.125,10.125 0 1,1 -20.25,0 Z" />
</vector>
